  "id": "gcp-mlops-training-promotion-v1",
  "title": "Continuous training pipeline with model validation and release gates",
  "subtitle": "A model-training pipeline validates data, transforms features, trains and evaluates candidates, and promotes an approved model to serving. Synthetic Azure reference; no deployment is implied.",
  "description": "### Problem\nRepeated model retraining needs consistent data validation, training and evaluation, reproducible artifacts, and a controlled route to online serving.\n\n### Flow and Azure mapping\nA data arrival or schedule triggers an Azure Machine Learning pipeline. It validates input data, transforms features, trains a candidate, evaluates it against criteria, and registers a versioned artifact. A release pipeline promotes a passing version into an inference environment such as managed online endpoints or AKS. Monitoring captures model and service signals and can inform future retraining decisions.\n\n### Trade-offs and assumptions\nThe Google source distinguishes continuous training on new data from CI/CD deployment of a changed pipeline implementation. Azure ML Pipelines and registries are candidates for the same responsibilities, but pipeline semantics and artifact formats differ. A promotion gate should not be implied to guarantee fairness, accuracy, or drift absence; the team must define measurable thresholds and human review where appropriate.\n\nSource: [Google Cloud Architecture Center](https://docs.cloud.google.com/architecture/architecture-for-mlops-using-tfx-kubeflow-pipelines-and-cloud-build?hl=en).\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- Origin provider: Google Cloud\n- Target: Azure conceptual adaptation\n- Primary source: [Architecture for MLOps using TFX, Vertex AI Pipelines, and Cloud Build](https://docs.cloud.google.com/architecture/architecture-for-mlops-using-tfx-kubeflow-pipelines-and-cloud-build?hl=en)\n- Reviewed: 2026-11-06\n\n## Supplementary context\n\n- [Best practices for implementing machine learning on Google Cloud](https://docs.cloud.google.com/architecture/ml-on-gcp-best-practices) — Reviewed: 2026-11-06; Supplementary provider context; not a copied diagram or implementation.\n\n## Catalog status\n\nThis is an original, editable Azure conceptual adaptation. It is synthetic reference material, not a deployed system, certified vendor architecture, or automatic deployment plan.\n\n## Mapping caveats\n\n- Model retraining on new data and redeployment of a changed pipeline are separate lifecycle paths.",
